{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {"HYPOTHESES.md": ["experiment_result"]}, "duration_s": 13899.1, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "1) E091 (T-0090, claimed here on this VM): hand-replicate E062's answerability sub-test on Anova cooking Discourse with pre-declared calibration gates, to test whether F096's 17-of-20 generalizes beyond Stack Exchange. 2) D099's head-to-head: real failing imports, three arms (pip install M, free general assistant, pyprovides forward mechanism) on the same cases, reusing E044's design. 3) Land this session's uncommitted artifacts in one commit.", "outcome": "partial", "push_requested": false, "summary": "E090 (T-0089) ran to a recorded verdict: the module-to-distribution reverse index over the 15000 most-downloaded PyPI projects resolves 618 of 1970 real imported module names (0.3137) against a declared 0.70 kill gate, with a decelerating K-curve; pip install M plus the index together answer 0.3893. G0 discrimination passed first (19/21, 0/30, 9/10). G3 passed at 0.0589 but is an upper bound because the protocol named three baselines and ran one (D099). D098 retires the index at any K; F111 records the finding; DECISIONS-SCREENING-18.md and FAILURES-findings-37.md are written; pyprovides/README.md is corrected in place. analyze.py reproduces every gate figure offline. The second half of the session goal (the head-to-head on real failing imports) was not run: D099 promotes it to the next experiment, and T-0090 (E091, demand-side hand replication of E062 on Anova cooking Discourse) was created and claimed but not started.", "unlogged_changes": 18}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 71, "session": "2026-10-10-006-decide-by-measurement-whether-which-dist", "ts": "2026-10-10T06:42:00+00:00"}
